{
  "title": "14: Ibrahim ابراهيم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالۤرٰ كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ اِلَيْكَ لِتُخْرِجَ النَّاسَ مِنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ  ۙ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِۙ‏(1)\nAR-RAA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO ELAYKA LETUKHREJA NAASA MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL NOORE BE-IZNIL RABBEHIM ELAA SERAATE A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nAlif, Lam, Ra, (A. L. R.) A Book (the Qur’an) (We) sent it down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) that thou mayest lead out men from the darkness into the light, by their Lord’s permission, unto the way of the Mighty, the (Most) Praised (One),\nاللّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَوَيْلٌ لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مِنْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدِ ۙ‏(2)\nLAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WAYLUL LIL-KAAFEREEN MIN A’ZAABIN SHADEEDE.\n(Of) God (it is) unto whom belongeth whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; and woe unto the dis believers for a severe torment,\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَحِبُّوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا عَلَى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YASTAHEBBOONA HAYAATAD DUNYAA A’LAL AAKHERATE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAYABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN AOOLAAEKA FEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nThose who love the life of this world more than the here after, and hinder (others) from the path of God and seek it to be crooked; these are in error far away (from the right path).\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا بِلِسَانِ قَوْمِهٖ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْؕ فَيُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(4)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA BELESAANE QAWMEHI LEEBAYNA LAHUM FA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nAnd We sent not any apostle but with the language of the people that he might clearly explain (Our commandments) unto them; then God leaveth to stray whom He willeth and guideth He whom He willeth, and He is the Mighty the Wise.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اَنْ اَخْرِجْ قَوْمَكَ مِنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ ۙ وَذَكِّرْهُمْ بِاَيّٰٮمِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍ‏(5)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA AN AAKHREJ QAWMAKA MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL NOORE WAZAKKERHUM BEAAYME LAAH INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nAnd indeed sent We Moses with Our signs saying: “Lead Thou out thy people from the darkness into the light and remind them of the days of God; Verily in this are signs for the patient, grateful (one).\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهِ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ اَنْجٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُوْمُوْنَكُمْ سُوْۤءَ الْعَذَابِ وَ يُذَبِّحُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُوْنَ نِسَآءَكُمْ ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ بَلَاۤ ءٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيْمٌ‏(6)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LEQAWMEHE KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ AANJAAKUM MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YASOOMOONAKUM SOOA A’ZAABE WA YOZABBEHOONA ABNAAA-AKUM WA YAS-TAHYOONA NESAAAKUM WA FEE ZAA ZAALEKUM BALAA UN MIN RABBEKUM A’ZEEM.\nAnd when said Moses unto his people; “Remember ye God’s favour unto you when He delivered you from Pharaoh’s people who afflicted you with dreadful torment, who were slaying your sons and sparing your women; and in this was a great trial from your Lord.\nوَاِذْ تَاَذَّنَ رَبُّكُمْ لَئِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ لَاَزِيْدَنَّكُمْ وَلَئِنْ كَفَرْتُمْ اِنَّ عَذَابِىْ لَشَدِيْدٌ‏(7)\nWA IZ TAAZZANA RABBOKUM LAIL SHAKARTUM LAAZEEDANNAKUM WA LAIN KAFARTUM INNAL A’AZAABEAA KHAYRE.\nAnd when declared your Lord: “If ye be grateful I will increase (My favours) unto you, and if ye be ungrateful, Verily my torment is indeed severe.\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اِنْ تَكْفُرُوْۤا اَنْتُمْ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ۙ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَنِىٌّ حَمِيْدٌ‏(8)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA IN TAKFUROOA ANTUM WA MAN FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A FA-INNAL LAAHA LA-GHANIYYUN HAMEED.\nAnd said Moses: “If ye be ungrateful, ye and those on earth, all together, verily God is the Absolute (Self-sufficient) the (Ever) Praised.\nاَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ نَبَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ  ۛؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ ۛؕ لَا يَعْلَمُهُمْ اِلَّا اللّٰهُؕ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَرَدُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمْ فِىْۤ اَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كَفَرْنَا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ وَاِنَّا لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ مُرِيْبٍ‏(9)\nALAM YAATEKUM NABAUA LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WAL LAZEENA MIN BA’DEHIM LAA YAA’LAMUHUM ILLAA LAAH JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FARADDOOA AYDEYAHUM FEE AFWAA-HEHIM WA QAALOO INNAA KAFARNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI WA INNAA LAFEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA TADU’OONANAA ELAYHE MOREEB.\nWhat! came not unto you the account of those before you, of the people of Noah, and ‘Ad, and Thamud; and those who (came) after them? None knoweth them but God; Came unto them their apostles with clear signs (miracles) but they thrust their hands into their mouths and said they “Verily we disbelieve (that) which ye are sent with and verily we are indeed in a doubt about that unto which ye invite us (which is) disquieting.\nقَالَتْ رُسُلُهُمْ اَفِى اللّٰهِ شَكٌّ فَاطِرِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يَدْعُوْكُمْ لِيَغْفِرَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُنُوْبِكُمْ وَيُؤَخِّرَكُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَاؕ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَصُدُّوْنَا عَمَّا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا فَاْتُوْنَا بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(10)\nQAALAT JAAA-ATHUM AAFEAA LAAHE SHAKKUN FAATERE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ YADU’OOKUM LEEGHFERA LAKUM MIN ZUNOOBEKUM WAYUAKKHERAKUM ELAA ELAA MOSAMMAA QAALOO IN ANTUM ILLAA BASHARUM MMESLUNAA TOREEDOONA AN TASUDDOONAA A’MMAA KAANA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA FAATOONAA BESULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nSaid their apostles! What! about God is there any doubt, the Originator of the heavens and the earth? He inviteth you to forgive for you your sins and grant you respite for a term appointed!” Said they: “Nothing are ye but men like unto us; ye intend that ye turn us away from what our fathers did worship, Therefore bring ye unto us some authority manifesting.\nقَالَتْ لَهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ اِنْ نَّحْنُ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَمُنُّ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖؕ وَمَا كَانَ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّاْتِيَكُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(11)\nQAALAT LAHUM JAAA-ATHUM IN NNAHNU ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAMUNNU A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’EBAADEH WA MAA KAANA LANAA AN NNAATEEKUM BESULTAANIM ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nSaid unto them their apostles: “(Yes) (nothing) we are but men like you but God bestoweth His favours whomsoever He willeth of His servants; and it is not for us that we bring unto you any authority except by the permission of God; And on God should the believers rely.\nوَمَا لَنَاۤ اَلَّا نَتَوَكَّلَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَقَدْ هَدٰٮنَا سُبُلَنَاؕ وَلَنَصْبِرَنَّ عَلٰى مَاۤ اٰذَيْتُمُوْنَاؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA MAA LANAA ALLAA NATAWAKKALA A’LAL LAAHE WA QAD HADAANAA SUBULANAA WALANASBERANNA A’LAA MAA AAAZAYTUMOONAA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\nAnd what reason have we that we should rely not on God, and indeed He hath guided us unto our ways; and surely we will endure whatever hurt ye may inflict on us; and on God (alone) should the reliant rely.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِرُسُلِهِمْ لَنُخْرِجَنَّكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِنَاۤ اَوْ لَتَعُوْدُنَّ فِىْ مِلَّتِنَا ؕ فَاَوْحٰۤى اِلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ لَنُهْلِكَنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(13)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LERUSULEHEM LANUKHREJANNAKUM MIN ARZENAA AW LATAU’OODUNNA FEE MELLATENAA FAAWHAA ELAYHIM RABBOHUM LANUHLEKANNA ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd said those who disbelieved unto their apostles: “Certainly will we drive you out of our land or else ye return to our religion.” So revealed unto them their Lord; “Certainly will We destroy the unjust ones.\nوَلَنُسْكِنَنَّكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ خَافَ مَقَامِىْ وَخَافَ وَعِيْدِ‏(14)\nWALANUSKENANNAKUMU ARZA MIN BAA’DEHEM ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y KHAAFA MAQAAMEAA WA KHAAFA WAE’EEDE.\nAnd certainly We will settle you in the land after them; This is for he who presence and who feareth My wrath.\nوَاسْتَفْتَحُوْا وَخَابَ كُلُّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍۙ‏(15)\nWAASTAFTAHOOA WA QAD KULLO JABBAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\nAnd sought they (the apostle’s) help (from God against their enemies), and every insolent rebellious one was disappointed,\nمِّنْ وَّرَآئِهٖ جَهَنَّمُ وَيُسْقٰى مِنْ مَّآءٍ صَدِيْدٍۙ‏(16)\nMIN WWARAAEH JAHANNAMUL WAYUSQAA MIN MAAA-IN SADEEDIN.\nBehind him is Hell and he shall be given to drink a festering water,\nيَّتَجَرَّعُهٗ وَلَا يَكَادُ يُسِيْغُهٗ وَيَاْتِيْهِ الْمَوْتُ مِنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ وَّمَا هُوَ بِمَيِّتٍؕ وَمِنْ وَّرَآئِهٖ عَذَابٌ غَلِيْظٌ‏(17)\nYYATAJARRAU’UH WA LAA YAKAADUL YUSEEGHUH WA YAATEEHIL MAWTO MIN KULLE MAKAANIN WA MAA HOWA BEMAYTIN WA MIN WWARAAEH A’ZAABUN GHALEEZUN.\nHe shall drink it little by little and shall not be able to swallow it, and will come unto him death from all sides but he shall die not; and shall be behind him a vehement torment.\nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ كَرَمَادِ ۨاشْتَدَّتْ بِهِ الرِّيْحُ فِىْ يَوْمٍ عَاصِفٍؕ لَا يَقْدِرُوْنَ مِمَّا كَسَبُوْا عَلٰى شَىْءٍؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الضَّلٰلُ الْبَعِيْدُ‏(18)\nMASALUL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM A-A’MAALOHUM KARAMAADE ASHTADDAT BEHIL AR-REEHU FEE YAWMIN A’AASEFIN LAA YAQDEROONA MIMMAA KASABOO A’LAA SHAYIN ZAA LEKA HOWA AZ-ZALAALU AL-BAE’EEDU.\nThe likeness of those who disbelieve in their Lord; their deeds are like ashes on which bloweth hard the wind on a stormy day; they shall not have any hold on anything of what they have earned; this is a far-gone wandering.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ وَيَاْتِ بِخَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍۙ‏(19)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ IN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM WA TAKOONOO BE-KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nSeest thou not that God created the heavens and the earth with truth? If He willeth He will take you away and bring (in your place) a creation anew,\nوَّمَا ذٰلِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(20)\nWA MAA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE BEA’AZEEZIN.\nAnd this for God is not difficult.\nوَبَرَزُوْا لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا فَقَالَ الضُّعَفٰۤؤُا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمْ تَبَعًا فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّغْنُوْنَ عَنَّا مِنْ عَذَابِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ قَالُوْا لَوْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ لَهَدَيْنٰكُمْؕ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَجَزِعْنَاۤ اَمْ صَبَرْنَا مَا لَنَا مِنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(21)\nWA BARAZOO LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A FAQAALA AZ-ZUA’AFAAUA LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KUNNAA LAKUM TABAA’AN FA HAL ANTUM MMUGHNOONA WAGH MIN A’ZAABIN LAAHE MIN SHAYIN QAALOO LAW HADAANAA LAAHO LAHADAYNAAKUM SAWAAA-UN A’LAYNAA AAJAZEA’NAA AM SABARNAA MAA LANAA MIN MAHEES.\nAnd they shall come forth before God all together, then shall say the weak unto those who were arrogant: “Verily we had been your followers, can ye therefore avert from us any part of the chastisement of God?” They would say: “If God hath guided us, we too would have surely guided you; it is the same to us (now) whether we implore (impatiently) or we are patient, (now) there is not for us (any) way of escape.\nوَقَالَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لَمَّا قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ وَعَدَكُمْ وَعْدَ الْحَقِّ وَوَعَدْتُّكُمْ فَاَخْلَفْتُكُمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِىَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ دَعَوْتُكُمْ فَاسْتَجَبْتُمْ لِىْ ۚ فَلَا تَلُوْمُوْنِىْ وَلُوْمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ ؕ مَاۤ اَنَا بِمُصْرِخِكُمْ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُصْرِخِىَّ ؕ اِنِّىْ كَفَرْتُ بِمَاۤ اَشْرَكْتُمُوْنِ مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(22)\nWA QAALA SHAYTAANO LAMMAA QUZEAAA MIN INNAL LAAHA WAA’ADAKUM WA’DAL HAQQE WAWAA’ADTTUKUM FAAKHLAFTUKUM WA MAA KAANA LEYA A’LAYKUM MIN SULTAANIN ILLAA AN DAA’AWTUKUM FAASTAJABTUM LEE FALAA TALOOMOONEAA WALOOMOOA ANFOSAKUM MAA ANAA BEMUSREKHEKUM WA MAA ANTUM BEMUSREKHEAAAA INNEE KAFARTU BEMAA AASHRAKTUMOONE MIN QABLO INNAL ZAALEMEEN LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAnd shall say Satan after the affair is decided: “Verily God promised you the promise of truth, and I gave you promises but failed to keep them to you; and I had no authority over you except I called you and ye responded unto me; so blame me not but (rather) blame yourselves; I cannot be your aider (now), nor can ye be my aiders; Verily I disbelieved in your associating me with God from before; Verily the unjust ones, for them shall be a painful chastisement.\nوَاُدْخِلَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِمْؕ تَحِيَّتُهُمْ فِيْهَا سَلٰمٌ‏(23)\nWAADKHELA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA BE-IZNIL RABBEHIM TAHIYYATOHUM FEEHAA SALAAMUN.\nAnd will be admitted those who believe and do good deeds to Gardens (of bliss) beneath which flow rivers, to abide in them by the permission of their Lord; their greeting therein will be ‘Salam’ (Peace).\nاَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ ضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا كَلِمَةً طَيِّبَةً كَشَجَرَةٍ طَيِّبَةٍ اَصْلُهَا ثَابِتٌ وَّفَرْعُهَا فِى السَّمَآءِۙ‏(24)\nALAM TARA KAYFA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA KALEMATAN TAYBATAN KASHAJARATIN TAYBATIN AASLUHAA SAABETUN WWAFARU’UHAA FIL SAMAAA-E.\nSeest thou not how setteth forth God a parable? of a goodly word (being) like a goodly tree, whose root is firmly fixed, and its branches (reach) heavens, in the heavens,\nتُؤْتِىْۤ اُكُلَهَا كُلَّ حِيْنٍۢ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهَاؕ وَيَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْاَمْثَالَ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(25)\nTUTEAA OKOLAHAA KULLA HEEN BE-IZNIL RABBEHAA WAYAZREBU LAAHO AL-AAMSAALA LIN-NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nYielding its fruit on every moment by the permission of its Lord. And setteth forth God parables for the people that they may reflect.\nوَمَثَلُ كَلِمَةٍ خَبِيْثَةٍ كَشَجَرَةٍ خَبِيْثَةٍۨاجْتُثَّتْ مِنْ فَوْقِ الْاَرْضِ مَا لَهَا مِنْ قَرَارٍ‏(26)\nWA MASALUL KALEMATIN KHABEESATIN KASHAJARATIN KHABEESATINAJTUSSAT MIN FAWQE ARZE MAA LAHAA MIN QARAARIN.\nAnd the parable of an evil word is that of an evil tree rooted upon the surface of the earth, it hast naught of stability.\nيُثَبِّتُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِالْقَوْلِ الثَّابِتِ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَيُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ ۙ وَيَفْعَلُ اللّٰهُ مَا يَشَآءُ‏(27)\nYUSABBETU LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-QAWLE AS-SAABETE FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA AAKHERATE WA YOZILLO LAAHO ZAALEMEEN WA YAF-A’LO LAAHO MAA YASHAAA.\nEstablisheth God (in strength) those who believe, with the firm word in the life of this world and in the hereafter; and God leaveth the unjust ones to stray; and doeth God what He willeth.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ بَدَّلُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ كُفْرًا وَّاَحَلُّوْا قَوْمَهُمْ دَارَ الْبَوَارِۙ‏(28)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA BADDALOO NEA’MATAL LAAHE KUFRAN WWAAHALLOOA QAWMAHUM DAARA AL-BAWAARE.\nHast thou not seen those who have exchanged God’s bounties with ingratitude and halted their people down into the abode of perdition,\nجَهَنَّمَۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَاؕ وَبِئْسَ الْقَرَارُ‏(29)\nJAHANNAMA YASLAWNAHAA WA BEASAL AL-QARAARU.\nHell! shall they enter into it; and an evil place (it is) to stay in!\nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا لِّيُضِلُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖؕ قُلْ تَمَتَّعُوْا فَاِنَّ مَصِيْرَكُمْ اِلَى النَّارِ‏(30)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE ANDAADANW LLEEZELLOOA A’N SABEELEH QUL TAMATTAU’OOA FA-INNAL MASEERAKUM ELAL NAAR.\nAnd they set up (idols as) equals to God that they may lead people astray from His path. Say! thou “Enjoy ye (your pleasures yet a while) for your return is unto the (Hell) fire.\nقُلْ لِّعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يُقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُنْفِقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ يَوْمٌ لَّا بَيْعٌ فِيْهِ وَلَا خِلٰلٌ‏(31)\nQUL LLEE’EBAADEAAA LAZEENA AAMANOO YUQEEMOOA SALAATA WAYUNFEQOOA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM SIRRAN WA A’LAANEYATAN MIN QABLE AN YAATEYA YAWMUL LAA BAY-U’N FEEHE WA LAA KHELAALUN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto My servants who believe that they should establish prayer and spend (in charity) secretly and openly, out of what We have given them, ere cometh the day in which there shall be no bargaining nor mutual befriending.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَاَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَخْرَجَ بِهٖ مِنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْفُلْكَ لِتَجْرِىَ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِاَمْرِهٖۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْاَنْهٰرَۚ‏(32)\nALLAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ANZALA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AKHRAJA BEHI MENAL SAMARAATE RIZQAN LAKUM SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL AL-FULKA LETAJREAAA FIL BAHRE LAAHO SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL AL-AANHAARA.\nGod is He who created the heavens and earth, and sent down from the heavens water, then brought forth with it fruits as sustenance for you; and subjected for you the ships that they may sail in the sea by His command; and subjected for you the rivers.\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ دَآئِبَيْنِۚ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَۚ‏(33)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL SHAMSA WAL QAMARA DAAEBAYNE SAKHKHARASH LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA.\nAnd He hath subject for you the sun and the moon pursuing their {respective) courses; and He hath subject for you the night and the day.\nوَاٰتٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ مَا سَاَلْتُمُوْهُ ؕ وَاِنْ تَعُدُّوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ لَا تُحْصُوْهَا ؕ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَظَلُوْمٌ كَفَّارٌ‏(34)\nWA AATAAKUM MIN KULLE MAA SAALTUMOOHU WA TAU’UDDOOA NEA’MATAL LAAHE LAA TUHSOOHAA INNAL INSAANA LAZALOOMUN KAFFAARUN.\nAnd He giveth you of every thing what ye ask Him; and if ye reckon God’s bounties ye will not be able to compute them; Verily man is very unjust; and very ungrateful.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هٰذَا الْبَلَدَ اٰمِنًا وَّاجْنُبْنِىْ وَبَنِىَّ اَنْ نَّعْبُدَ الْاَصْنَامَؕ‏(35)\nWA IZ QAALA AEBRAAHEEMU RABBE A’L HAAZAA AL-BALADA AAMENANW WWAAJNUBNEAA WABANEAAAA AN NNAA’BUDA AL-AASNAAMA.\nAnd when said Abraham: “My Lord! make this city secure, and keep me away and my sons from worshipping idols.\nرَبِّ اِنَّهُنَّ اَضْلَلْنَ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِۚ فَمَنْ تَبِعَنِىْ فَاِنَّهٗ مِنِّىْۚ وَمَنْ عَصَانِىْ فَاِنَّكَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(36)\nRABBE AENNAHUNNA AAZLALNA KASEERAA MENAL NAASE FAMAN TABEA’ANEAA FA-INNAHU MINNEE WA MAN A’ASAANEAA FA-INNAKA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nMy Lord! Verily they have led many of the people astray; so whosoever followeth me he is surely of me, and who soever disobeyeth me, then verily Thou art the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْكَنْتُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِىْ زَرْعٍ عِنْدَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِۙ رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيْمُوْا الصَّلٰوةَ فَاجْعَلْ اَ فْئِدَةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ وَارْزُقْهُمْ مِّنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(37)\nRABBANAA INNEE AASKANTU MIN ZURREETEAA BEWAADIN GHAIRE ZEE ZARA’IN I’NDAL BAYTEKA AL-MUHARRAME RABBANAA LEEQEEMOOA SALAATA FAJ-A’L A’ZAABAN FEDATAN MENAL NAASE TAHWEAA ELAYHIM WAARZUQHUM MENAL SAMARAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YASHKOROON.\nO’ Our Lord! Verily I have housed a part of my offspring in a valley uncultivable, nigh unto Thy Holy House, Our Lord! that they may establish prayer; so make Thou the hearts of some of the people yearn unto them, and provide them with fruits, that they may be grateful.\nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ تَعْلَمُ مَا نُخْفِىْ وَمَا نُعْلِنُ ؕ وَمَا يَخْفٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ‏(38)\nRABBANAA INNAKA TAA’LAMU MAA NUKHFEAA WA MAA NUA’LENU WA MAA YAKHFAA A’LAL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN FIL ARZE WA LAA FIL SAMAAA-E.\nO’ Our Lord! Verily Thou knowest what we hide and what we manifest and is not hidden from God, of any thing in the earth, and nor (any thing) in the heaven (is hidden from Him)\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ وَهَبَ لِىْ عَلَى الْكِبَرِ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَسَمِيْعُ الدُّعَآءِ‏(39)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE WAHABA LEE A’LAL AL-KEBARE AESMAAE’EELA WAASHAAQA INNAL RABBEE LASAMEEU’U AD-DUA’AAE.\nPraise is God’s, Who hath granted unto me in old age, Ishmael and Isaac: Verily my Lord is the Hearer of Prayer.\nرَبِّ اجْعَلْنِىْ مُقِيْمَ الصَّلٰوةِ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ ۖ  رَبَّنَا وَتَقَبَّلْ دُعَآءِ‏(40)\nRABBE AJA’ALNEAA MUQEEMA AS-SALAAWTE WA MIN ZURREETEAA RABBANAA WA RABBANAA DO-A’AA-IL.\nO’ my Lord! make me establish prayer and (also) some from my offspring (to do the same); O’ Our Lord! accept thou my prayer!\nرَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لِىْ وَلِوَالِدَىَّ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ يَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْحِسَابُ‏(41)\nRABBANAA FIR LEE WALEWAALEDAA LIL-MOAMENEENA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUL AL-HESAABU.\nO’ Our Lord! Forgive me and my parents and the believers on the day when the reckoning shall be established!\nوَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَافِلًا عَمَّا يَعْمَلُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ ؕ اِنَّمَا يُؤَخِّرُهُمْ لِيَوْمٍ تَشْخَصُ فِيْهِ الْاَبْصَارُ ۙ‏(42)\nWA LAA TAHSABANNA LAAHA GHAAFELAN A’MMAA YAA’MALU ZAALEMOON INNAMAA YUAKKHERUHUM LE-YAWMIN TASHKHASU FEEHE IZ ZAAGHATIL.\nAnd think not God to be heedless of what the unjust ones do. He only respiteth them to a day when the eyes shall be fixed open (staring up with terror),\nمُهْطِعِيْنَ مُقْنِعِىْ رُءُوْسِهِمْ لَا يَرْتَدُّ اِلَيْهِمْ طَرْفُهُمْ ۚ وَاَفْئِدَتُهُمْ هَوَآءٌ ؕ‏(43)\nMUHTEE’EENA MUQNEE’EAA RUOOSEHEM LAA YARTADDU ELAYHIM TARFUHUM WAAFEDATUHUM HAWAAUN.\nRunning on with fear, their heads upraised, their eyes not reverting unto them and the hearts blank.\nوَاَنْذِرِ النَّاسَ يَوْمَ يَاْتِيْهِمُ الْعَذَابُ فَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَخِّرْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ نُّجِبْ دَعْوَتَكَ وَنَتَّبِعِ الرُّسُلَؕ اَوَلَمْ تَكُوْنُوْۤااَقْسَمْتُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ مَالَكُمْ مِّنْ زَوَالٍۙ‏(44)\nWAANZERE NAASA YAWMA YAATEEHEMU A’ZAABO FAYAQOOLO LAZEENA ZALAMOO RABBANAA AAKKHERNAA ELAA ELAA QAREEBIN NNUJEB DAA’WATAKA WANATTABEE’E AR-RUSULA AWALAM TAKOONOOAAAQSAMTUM MIN QABLO MAALAKUM MIN ZAWAALIN.\nAnd warn thou the people, of the day when shall come unto them the chastisement, then will say those who did injustice “O’ Our Lord! respite us yet for a short term, (that) we may respond unto Thy call and follow the apostles.” What! Were ye not wont to swear aforetime that there will not be for you any decline,\nوَّسَكَنْتُمْ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمْ كَيْفَ فَعَلْنَا بِهِمْ وَضَرَبْنَا لَكُمُ الْاَمْثَالَ‏(45)\nWWASAKANTUM FEE MASAAKENE LAZEENA ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM WA TABAYYANA LAKUM KAYFA FAA’ALNAA BEHIM WA ZARABNAA LAKOMUL AL-AAMSAALA.\nAnd ye dwelt in the abodes of those who did injustice unto themselves, and it was made clear unto you how We dealt with them and We have set forth examples for you.\nوَقَدْ مَكَرُوْا مَكْرَهُمْ وَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ مَكْرُهُمْؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مَكْرُهُمْ لِتَزُوْلَ مِنْهُ الْجِبَالُ‏(46)\nWA QAD MAKAROOA MAKRAHUM WA I’NDAL LAAHE MAKRUHUM WA KAANA MAKRUHUM LETAZOOLA MINHO JEBAALO.\nAnd indeed they did devise their plots, but (all) within the view of God were their plots even though their plot was such (powerful one) as to move thereby mountains.\nفَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِفَ وَعْدِهٖ رُسُلَهٗؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ ذُوْ انْتِقَامٍؕ‏(47)\nFALAA TAHSABANNA LAAHA MUKHLEFA WAA’DEH RUSULAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN ZOO ANTEQAAMIN.\nAnd think ye not that God will fail His apostles in His promise; Verily God is Mighty, the Lord of Retribution.\nيَوْمَ تُبَدَّلُ الْاَرْضُ غَيْرَ الْاَرْضِ وَالسَّمٰوٰتُ وَبَرَزُوْا لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ‏(48)\nYAWMA TUBADDALU ARZO GHAYRA ARZE WAALSSAMAAWAATU WA BARAZOO LILLAAHE AL-WAAHEDE AL-QAHHAARE.\nOn the day when the earth shall be changed into a different earth, and (so will be) the heavens (too), and (all men) shall be marshalled forth unto God the One, the Dominant.\nوَتَرَى الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ يَوْمَئِذٍ مُّقَرَّنِيْنَ فِى الْاَصْفَادِۚ‏(49)\nWA TARAL MUJREMEEN YAWMA-EZIN MMUQARRANEENA FIL AL-AASFAADE.\nAnd thou wilt see the guilty (ones) on that day bound together in chains.\nسَرَابِيْلُهُمْ مِّنْ قَطِرَانٍ وَّتَغْشٰى وُجُوْهَهُمُ النَّارُۙ‏(50)\nSARAABEELUHUM MIN QATERAANIN WWATAGHSHAA WUJOOHAHUMU TAMASSANAN.\nTheir garments (shall be) of pitch and their faces covered with fire,\nلِيَجْزِىَ اللّٰهُ كُلَّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(51)\nLE-YAJZEYAL LAAHO KULLA NAFSIM MAA KASABAT INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThat God may recompense each soul (as) what it hath earned; Verily God is swift in reckoning.\nهٰذَا بَلٰغٌ لِّلنَّاسِ وَلِيُنْذَرُوْا بِهٖ وَلِيَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ وَّلِيَذَّكَّرَ اُولُوا الْا َلْبَابِ‏(52)\nHAAZAA BALAAGHUN LIN-NAASE WALEENZAROOA BEHI WALEEA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED WWALEEZZAKKARA ULUL AL-A LBAABE.\nThis is a clear message for the mankind and that they may be warned by it, that they may know that He is God, (the only) One and that the men of understanding may mind.",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah that has 52 verses. It is narrated by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah Ibrahim and [Surah Hijr](A19) in a two-rak’aat prayer on every Friday, he will remain safe from poverty, insanity and sudden calamity.\nIn Tafseer al-Burhan, it is mentioned that writing this Surah on a white parchment and then making a child wear it as a talisman keeps the child safe from ailments and makes it easy for him to drink and digest milk."
}
